#       constraint/rationale it documents (gate②'s review protocol, the freshness/OID-bound
#       rules, bot-login normalization) and drops the private predecessor-repo framing
#       (`pr_gate.sh`, "TS port of X", "predecessor-project-style"). No behavior change —
#       comment-only.
#
# WHY IT MATTERS: #841 (public-launch hygiene) scrubs references to the project's private
#       predecessor from production code and user-facing docs — a user browsing the shipped
#       repo has no access to that private repo, and a comment pointing at it only confuses.
#       See #841's PR body for the full file-by-file classification table.
#
# WHY IT IS A PATCH AND NOT A COMMIT: `reviewer.ts` is human-merge-only (docs/security.md
#       "Human-merge-only paths") — it is gate②'s review-verdict seam, enforced by the guard,
#       not by convention. An autonomous worker's write to it is denied at the tool level.
#
# APPLY (from the repo root), then delete this file:
#       git apply docs/patches/841-reviewer-archaeology-scrub.patch
#       git rm docs/patches/841-reviewer-archaeology-scrub.patch
#
